  "decision_conditions": [
    "Wildlife and Countryside Act 1981:  Note that it is an offence under this act to disturb roosting bats, nesting birds or any other protected species.  Therefore, if applicable, it is advisable to consult your tree surgeon / consultant to agree an acceptable time for carrying out the approved works.",
    "TPO 7 G32 1x Lime to fell.",
    "TPO 7 A4 1x Ash to reduce lateral overhang by up to 3m.",
    "The trees are situated in the school grounds. They are in a moderate condition and can be seen by students and visitors. For this reason they hold a moderate amenity value.",
    "The Lime has Ganoderma, but the Arboriculture Consultant has recommended pollarding as sufficient. Removing the tree would remove any amenity it has.",
    "We reject the specification to remove the Lime tree due to a lack of evidence and contradiction to professional opinion.",
    "The length of the lateral limbs of the tree to be pruned shall be tip-reduced as per the approved specification / by a maximum of 3 m. This work shall comprise a reduction in the length of the limb(s) in a uniform and systematic manner and the limb(s) should be cut back to suitably positioned secondary branches.",
    "The work shall result in a tree of typical form for the species and of balanced appearance. The level of limb reduction shall be expressed either as a percentage / length of the overall limb length to be removed, or as a level of clearance to be provided.",
    "The works shall be carried out in accordance with the recommendations contained in BS3998: 2010 - \"British Standard Recommendations for Tree Work\".  Climbing irons or 'spikes' shall not be used during the execution of the work.",
    "Reason",
    "In order to protect health of the tree and the visual amenity of the area."
  ],
